<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Experimental Settings</h3>

<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Models</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By following prior works <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite> we mainly evaluate our method on BLIP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite> and CLIP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite> that are initially fine-tuned by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite> for various downstream tasks.
We also extend our method to LLaVA-v1.5-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite> that represents the prevalent LLM-based VLMs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Datasets and Evaluation Metrics</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For task-specific VLMs, we evaluate CoMP on four datasets. Concretely, we report accuracy on the development (Dev. Acc.) and test (Test Acc.) sets of NLVR2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite> for the visual reasoning task. For image-text retrieval, we report the top-1/-5 recall, denoted by R@1/5, on COCO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite> and Flickr30K <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">65</a>]</cite>. CIDEr <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite> and SPICE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> on COCO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite> are presented for image captioning, and accuracy on the development (Test-dev) and standard (Test-std) sets of VQAv2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite> are reported for visual question answering.
As for LLaVA, pruning is conducted during training on the official 665K instruction data <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>. We evaluate methods on six widely used image understanding benchmarks, by reporting the sum of perception and cognition scores for MME <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>, accuracy for MMBench (denoted as MMB) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>, GQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>, TextVQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite> and VQAv2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>, and F1 score for POPE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>.
To demonstrate computational efficiency, we report the Floating-Point Operations (<em id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e</em>.<span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span> GFLOPs or TFLOPs) per sample during inference.
More detailed descriptions are provided in the <em id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Appendix</em>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T2.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S4.T2.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(<span id="S4.T2.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Top</span>) Comparison of R@1/5 (%) and GFLOPs for BLIP/CLIP on Flickr30K and COCO for the image-text retrieval task. (<span id="S4.T2.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bottom</span>) Comparison of CIDEr and SPICE on COCO for the image captioning task and Test-dev/std accuracy (%) on VQAv2 for the visual question answering task as well as GFLOPs, based on BLIP. ‘*’ indicates GFLOPs during inference by our re-implementation, which were not reported in the original works. The best results are highlighted in <span id="S4.T2.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>.</span></figcaption>
