<div id="algorithm1.6.45" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.45.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.45.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.45.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  </span>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.45.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">42</span></span>
          <math id="algorithm1.m70" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leftarrow\text{Random\_choice}(\text{Indices}(\mathcal{B}),\text{prob}=\{\rho_{0},\rho_{1},\rho_{2},\rho_{3},\rho_{4}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">Random_choice</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">Indices</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℬ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">prob</mtext><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leftarrow\text{Random\_choice}(\text{Indices}(\mathcal{B}),\text{prob}=\{\rho_{0},\rho_{1},\rho_{2},\rho_{3},\rho_{4}\})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.45.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.46" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.46.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.46.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  </span>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.46.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">43</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.6.46.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">else</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.47" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.47.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.47.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.47.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  </span>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.47.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">44</span></span>
          <math id="algorithm1.m71" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leftarrow\arg\min(\mathcal{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℛ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leftarrow\arg\min(\mathcal{R})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.47.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  
</span><span id="algorithm1.6.47.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;"># Select a priority pruning mode according to pruning cost</span><span id="algorithm1.6.47.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.48" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.48.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">45</span></span>
          <math id="algorithm1.m72" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{W}}\leftarrow\bm{W}\odot{\bm{M}^{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑾</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑾</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑴</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{W}}\leftarrow\bm{W}\odot{\bm{M}^{p}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.48.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  
</span><span id="algorithm1.6.48.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;"># Completely prune parameters according to the parameter mask</span><span id="algorithm1.6.48.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.49" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.49.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">46</span></span>
          <math id="algorithm1.m73" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta_{v}^{t}}\leftarrow\Theta_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo>^</mo></mover><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta_{v}^{t}}\leftarrow\Theta_{3}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.49.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><math id="algorithm1.m74" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta_{l}^{t}}\leftarrow\Theta_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">l</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo>^</mo></mover><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta_{l}^{t}}\leftarrow\Theta_{4}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.49.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.50" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.50.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">47</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.6.50.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">return</span><span id="algorithm1.6.50.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="algorithm1.m75" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{F}(\cdot|\hat{\bm{W}},\hat{\theta_{v}^{t}},\hat{\theta_{l}^{t}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℱ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑾</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo>^</mo></mover><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">l</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo>^</mo></mover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}(\cdot|\hat{\bm{W}},\hat{\theta_{v}^{t}},\hat{\theta_{l}^{t}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.50.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.51" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S1a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The overall workflow of our proposed CoMP is summarized in <a href="#algorithm1" title="In A Overall Algorithm of CoMP ‣ Collaborative Multi-Mode Pruning for Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
Lines <math id="S1a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="13\sim 30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo>∼</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">13\sim 30</annotation></semantics></math> describe the pipeline of inner loop as shown in <a href="#S1.F3.sf1" title="In Figure 3 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Collaborative Multi-Mode Pruning for Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(a)</span></a>, pruning parameters and tokens based on importance scores calculated by the CIM module. Lines <math id="S1a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8\sim 44" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>∼</mo><mn>44</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\sim 44</annotation></semantics></math> depict the pipeline of outer loop as displayed in <a href="#S1.F3.sf1" title="In Figure 3 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Collaborative Multi-Mode Pruning for Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(a)</span></a>, by periodically shifting pruning modes with random exploration and historical information.
Notably, <math id="S1a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math> training steps are performed between mode shifting. In the parameter pruning mode, this interval is evenly divided into six sub-intervals <math id="S1a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}\!=\!\mathcal{I}/6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}\!=\!\mathcal{I}/6</annotation></semantics></math>. For each of the first five sub-intervals, we accumulate parameter importance scores over the <math id="S1a.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}</annotation></semantics></math> steps to ensure training stability, and then uniformly decay the mask values <math id="S1a.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{M}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{M}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> from 1 to 0, by following the UPop <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite> framework. In the final <math id="S1a.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}</annotation></semantics></math> steps, only parameter updates are performed to enable model recovery.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2a" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">B </span>Detailed Description of Datasets and Evaluation Metrics</h2>

<div id="S2a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2a.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For task-specific VLMs, we primarily evaluate our proposed method on four widely used public datasets, including NLVR2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite>, COCO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>, Flickr30K <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">65</a>]</cite> and VQAv2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>.
We also include experiments on the MSR-VTT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>]</cite> dataset in this document.
For LLaVA, we further assess methods on six widely adopted image understanding benchmarks, including MME <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>, MMBench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>, GQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>, TextVQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite>, VQAv2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite> and POPE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>. In addition, the pruning is conducted through supervised fine-tuning (SFT) on the official 665K instruction data <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite> (denoted as Mix665K).</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">NLVR2</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The NLVR2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite> dataset is designed for the advancement of joint reasoning over natural language and images.
It contains <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="29{,}680" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>29,680</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">29{,}680</annotation></semantics></math> sentences and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="127{,}502" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>127,502</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">127{,}502</annotation></semantics></math> real-world images, which are combined to form <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="107{,}292" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>107,292</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">107{,}292</annotation></semantics></math> examples.
Each example consists of a caption text paired with two images, and the task is to determine whether the caption accurately describes both images.
The overall examples are divided into training, development, public test and unreleased test sets, which contain <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="86{,}373" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>86,373</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">86{,}373</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6{,}982" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6,982</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6{,}982</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6{,}967" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6,967</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6{,}967</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6{,}970" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6,970</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6{,}970</annotation></semantics></math> examples, respectively.
We report the accuracy on the development set (Dev. Acc.) and the public test set (Test Acc.) as the evaluation metric.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">COCO</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The COCO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite> dataset is a widely used benchmark that facilitates multiple tasks by promoting the scene understanding capability. Each image is annotated with 5 captions.
In our work, by following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>, we adopt the Karpathy split for both image-text retrieval and image captioning tasks, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\emph{i.e.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\emph{i.e.}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="113" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>113</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">113</annotation></semantics></math>K, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>K and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>K images for training, validation and test, respectively.
In the image-text retrieval task, as the goal is to retrieve the most relevant image/text given an input query, we report the top-1/-5 recall (R@1/5) as the evaluation metric.
In the image captioning task, as this task aims to generate a descriptive sentence that accurately reflects the visual content of a given image, we report CIDEr <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite> and SPICE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> as the evaluation metrics. Concretely,
CIDEr <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite> evaluates the quality of the generated captions by measuring their consensus with multiple reference sentences. SPICE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> simulates the human judgment process by comparing the semantic propositional content.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Flickr30K</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Flickr30K <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">65</a>]</cite> dataset is originally designed for visual denotation. We also adopt the Karpathy split on the image-text retrieval task and report the top-1/-5 recall (R@1/5) metrics for evaluation.
The training, validation and test sets consist of <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="29" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>29</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">29</annotation></semantics></math>K, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>K and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>K images, respectively, where each image has 5 captions.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S2.T1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Table A</span>: </span><span id="S2.T1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Training and testing configurations for pruning BLIP, CLIP and LLaVA models on various vision-language tasks. ‘Reasoning’, ‘Retrieval’, ‘Captioning’, ‘VQA’, ‘Und’ denote the visual reasoning task, the image-text retrieval task, the image captioning task, the visual question answering task and the image understanding task, respectively. <math id="S2.T1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{R}_{\text{I}\rightarrow\text{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>R</mtext><mrow><mtext>I</mtext><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext>T</mtext></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{R}_{\text{I}\rightarrow\text{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.T1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{R}_{\text{T}\rightarrow\text{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>R</mtext><mrow><mtext>T</mtext><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext>I</mtext></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{R}_{\text{T}\rightarrow\text{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the recall for image-to-text and text-to-image retrieval, respectively. <math id="S2.T1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\text{Val\_Loss}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mtext>Val_Loss</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\text{Val\_Loss}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the negative of the loss on validation set. ‘-’ indicates that the setting is not applied to the corresponding task.</span></figcaption>
