<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">VQAv2</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The VQAv2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite> dataset is curated for the visual question answering task.
Given an image and a question, this task encourages the model to jointly understand and reason over all information and generate a short answer.
For the BLIP model, by following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>, we adopt the split consisting of <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="123" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>123</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">123</annotation></semantics></math>K images and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="658" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>658</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">658</annotation></semantics></math>K questions for training, and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="81" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>81</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">81</annotation></semantics></math>K images and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="448" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>448</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">448</annotation></semantics></math>K questions for testing. We report accuracy on both the development (Test-dev) and standard (Test-std) splits of the test set.
For the LLaVA model, by following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>, we conduct zero-shot evaluation and report accuracy on the development split of the test set.
All metrics are obtained through the official evaluation website.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">MSR-VTT</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The MSR-VTT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>]</cite> dataset is a large-scale video description benchmark with comprehensive categories and varied video content. It contains <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math>K video clips, each paired with 20 human-annotated textual descriptions. We follow the evaluation protocol of the BLIP model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite> to perform zero-shot video-text retrieval and report the top-1/-5 recall (R@1/5) metrics on the <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>K test split.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2604.02956v1/illustration_llava.png" id="S2.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:583/226;" width="583" height="226" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure A</span>: </span><span id="S2.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Illustration of extending CoMP to the LLaVA-style architecture. We perform pruning in the LLM component, including pruning of vision tokens, language tokens and parameters, since this part accounts for more than 95% of the overall FLOPs.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">MME</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The MME <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite> dataset assesses a model’s perception and cognition capabilities. It consists of 14 sub-tasks with <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> questions for perception and 800 for cognition, where each image is associated with two binary (Yes/No) queries. By following existing works <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>, <a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>, <a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>]</cite>, we report the summation of scores on both capabilities. For the average score in <a href="#S4.T3" title="In On Image Captioning Task ‣ 4.2 Main Results on Vision-Language Tasks ‣ 4 Experimental Results and Analysis ‣ Collaborative Multi-Mode Pruning for Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, the summation is normalized by dividing by <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2{,}800" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2,800</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2{,}800</annotation></semantics></math>, which corresponds to the full score.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">MMBench</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The MMBench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite> dataset provides a balanced and comprehensive evaluation of model capabilities across three hierarchical levels. It consists of <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3{,}217" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3,217</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3{,}217</annotation></semantics></math> multiple-choice questions, with the dataset split into development and test subsets at a <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4{:}6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4{:}6</annotation></semantics></math> ratio. By following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>, we report the accuracy on the development set by submitting predictions to the official evaluation server.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px8" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">GQA</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The GQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite> dataset targets visual understanding and reasoning capabilities in complex real-world scenarios. It contains binary and open queries across real-world reasoning, scene understanding, and compositional question answering. In line with the compared methods, we perform evaluation on the ‘testdev’ subset from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>, which contains <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12{,}578" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>12,578</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12{,}578</annotation></semantics></math> questions, and report the standard accuracy.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px9" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">TextVQA</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The TextVQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite> dataset assesses a model’s ability to understand and reason over text present within images. The benchmark requires the model to read textual content from images and answer associated open-ended questions. We report accuracy on the validation split, which comprises <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> image-question pairs.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2604.02956v1/dim_map.png" id="S2.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:651/105;" width="651" height="105" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure B</span>: </span><span id="S2.F2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Illustration of the dimension mapping for parameter pruning in FFN (Left) and MHA (Right).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S2.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2604.02956v1/flops_contribution.png" id="S2.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:651/66;" width="651" height="66" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure C</span>: </span><span id="S2.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">FLOPs contributions of different pruning modes for the BLIP model, evaluated on the NLVR2 dataset at a pruning ratio of 0.85.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S2.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S2.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table C</span>: </span><span id="S2.T3.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of GFLOPs, Latency (ms per image) and Speedup Ratio across various pruning methods on BLIP using NLVR2 dataset at a pruning ratio of 0.85. Best results are highlighted in <span id="S2.T3.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S2.T3.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S2.T3.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T3.6.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="S2.T3.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span><span id="S2.T3.6.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> <span id="S2.T3.6.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text">
<span id="S2.T3.6.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="S2.T3.6.1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S2.T3.6.1.1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">Method</span></span>
</span></span><span id="S2.T3.6.1.1.2.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span></td>
